From d067996d56293830662c20d9ff82a87b7e47b2ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mohamed Gad <mohamedgad.tg@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:35:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] Train curricula in strict CSV order with exact resume

With data.shuffle: false a run is a single pass over the CSV in order:
- ResumableSequentialSampler yields rows in order (no wrap-around padding)
  and resumes at the row after the last checkpoint instead of row 0
- a row that fails to load is retried, then fails the run; it is never
  replaced by a random row, and a failed batch is never skipped
- training ends when the list is exhausted (optimization.epochs: auto)
- data.per_clip_rng seeds each clip's window/crop/flip by its path and each
  batch's masks by its first row, so curricula differ only in order
- log_r0.csv also records step, batch rows, prediction/context losses,
  context-loss weight and lr

Also read the encoder width from the model (vit_base crashed), make the
context-loss ramp configurable (model.lambda_start_iter / lambda_end_iter;
the hard-coded 15k-30k is never reached in a short run) and drop a
per-sample debug print.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
